1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,500
Action Movie Icons — Then & Now

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,710
Welcome to Action Icons, Then and Now.

3
00:00:14,810 --> 00:00:20,329
Arnold Schwarzenegger turned a champion
bodybuilder's physical presence into an
unmistakable movie persona.

4
00:00:20,429 --> 00:00:29,962
The Terminator, Predator, and Total Recall made him
a symbol of eighties action, while later work added
comedy and public service to the story.

5
00:00:30,062 --> 00:00:33,976
Sylvester Stallone created two of cinema's most
durable underdogs.

6
00:00:34,076 --> 00:00:42,004
Rocky and Rambo began as very different characters,
but both carried the determination that made his
screen image so lasting.

7
00:00:42,104 --> 00:00:46,017
Harrison Ford brought a dry, grounded humor to
extraordinary adventures.

8
00:00:46,117 --> 00:00:54,045
Han Solo and Indiana Jones remain legendary because
he made heroes look brave, skeptical, and human at
the same time.

9
00:00:54,145 --> 00:00:58,059
These early and later portraits span more than
changing hairstyles.

10
00:00:58,159 --> 00:01:01,370
They capture how action stardom learned to endure.

11
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:07,272
The next icons prove that action can take many
forms.

12
00:01:07,372 --> 00:01:15,402
Samuel L Jackson can turn a few lines into a
defining movie moment, from Pulp Fiction to Nick
Fury and beyond.

13
00:01:15,502 --> 00:01:19,661
His voice, timing, and presence make even an
ensemble feel larger.

14
00:01:19,761 --> 00:01:27,404
Hugh Jackman brought musical theater energy and
fierce physical commitment to Wolverine, then
showed another side in The Greatest Showman.

15
00:01:27,504 --> 00:01:35,148
Sigourney Weaver changed science fiction with
Ripley in Alien, a character defined by
intelligence and survival rather than easy
stereotypes.

16
00:01:35,248 --> 00:01:38,632
Ghostbusters and Avatar later displayed her comedy
and imagination.

17
00:01:38,732 --> 00:01:42,891
Six action careers, each built on a different kind
of strength.

18
00:01:42,991 --> 00:01:47,250
Which hero or heroine would you add to the next
chapter?

19
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,000
The close-up chapter begins. Look again at the portraits, the years, and the roles.

20
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:31,600
Which early and later pairing surprised you most?

21
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:59,600
